# architecture

- label: pace is a self-hostable personal dashboard — single container, no external services required beyond optional LLM
  command: grep -q 'pace' package.json
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: backend is TypeScript on Bun with Hono as the web framework — entry point is src/index.ts
  command: test -f src/index.ts && grep -q 'Hono' src/index.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: data is stored in a single SQLite database via bun:sqlite — schema defined in src/db.ts
  command: test -f src/db.ts && grep -q 'bun:sqlite' src/db.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: frontend is server-rendered HTML via Hono JSX — no client-side framework, only vanilla JS for interactivity
  command: grep -rq 'hono/jsx' src/
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: app ships with a Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml — docker compose up starts the full stack
  command: test -f Dockerfile && test -f docker-compose.yml
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: all transforms run at ingest time in the scheduler — DB contains final cleaned data, request handler just reads and renders
  command: grep -q 'runPipeline' src/scheduler.ts && ! grep -q 'runPipeline' src/index.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: pipelines are cross-adapter transform chains — defined in config under pipelines section, results stored under the panel ID of the panel that references the pipeline
  command: grep -q 'PipelineConfig' src/config.ts && grep -q 'runPipelineJob' src/scheduler.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: items are stored per panel ID — the panel_id column in content_items is the primary storage and query key
  command: grep -q 'panel_id TEXT NOT NULL' src/db.ts && grep -q 'getItemsByPanel' src/db.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: panel ID can be set explicitly via the id field in panel config — if not set, a hash of the panel config (name, source, limit) is used
  command: grep -q 'id.*string' src/config.ts && grep -q 'resolvePanelId' src/config.ts && grep -q 'CryptoHasher' src/config.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: panel ID uniqueness is validated at config load time — both explicit and hash-derived IDs must be unique across all panels
  command: grep -q 'duplicate panel ID' src/config.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: getDb in src/db.ts supports PACE_DB_PATH env var override (default remains cwd/data/pace.db); enables hermetic /tmp DBs for tests without cwd pollution (verifier-path.ts PASS)
  command: PACE_DB_PATH=/tmp/pace-fact-db-custom/data/pace.db bun --cwd /tmp/pace-fact-cwd /tmp/bugbash-db-20260521-020315/evidence/verifier-path.ts 2>&1 | grep -q 'PATH_VERIFIER_PASS'
  tags: [bugbash-iter10, implemented]
- label: closeDb in src/db.ts resets the module singleton (db=null) so subsequent getDb/save/get reuse succeeds without 'Cannot use a closed database' error (verifier-close.ts PASS)
  command: bun --cwd /tmp/pace-fact-close /tmp/bugbash-db-20260521-020315/evidence/verifier-close.ts 2>&1 | grep -q 'CLOSE_VERIFIER_PASS'
  tags: [bugbash-iter10, implemented]
- label: dedup logic (getRecentItems/getItemsByPanel/getAllItemsByPanel) in src/db.ts uses normalized url key (lower + rtrim trailing /) and max(timestamp) selection for consistency; getAll now dedups like others (verifier-dedup.ts with case/uni PASS)
  command: bun --cwd /tmp/pace-fact-dedup /tmp/bugbash-db-20260521-020315/evidence/verifier-dedup.ts 2>&1 | grep -q 'DEDUP_VERIFIER_PASS'
  tags: [bugbash-iter10, implemented]
- label: saveItems (and init) wrap sqlite/JS errors with 'db:' prefix + context for clear surfacing (e.g. 'db: failed to save...'); bad inputs no longer leak raw 'toISOString is not' or bare SQLiteError (verifier-error.ts PASS)
  command: bun --cwd /tmp/pace-fact-err /tmp/bugbash-db-20260521-020315/evidence/verifier-error.ts 2>&1 | grep -q 'ERROR_VERIFIER_PASS'
  tags: [bugbash-iter10, implemented]
- label: pruneOldItems(days?: number) is exported from src/db.ts, deletes rows with fetched_at older than N days, returns change count (verifier-prune.ts PASS)
  command: bun --cwd /tmp/pace-fact-prune /tmp/bugbash-db-20260521-020315/evidence/verifier-prune.ts 2>&1 | grep -q 'PRUNE_VERIFIER_PASS'
  tags: [bugbash-iter10, implemented]
- config.ts duplicated inline non-empty string validation logic (the `typeof x !== "string" || x.trim().length === 0` patterns appearing in validateSource, validateLayoutNode, validateStringList, validateKeywordScoreEntries, validateTransforms, validateTransform, validateAdapterConfig, validatePipelineConfig) is extracted to a single validateNonEmptyString helper (symmetric to existing validateOptionalNonEmptyString); all 9+ call sites delegate to it preserving exact error messages and behavior; src/config.test.ts guards exported helpers (normalizeSource/collectPanels/resolvePanelId/isPanel/isContainer) and loadConfig validation paths (non-empty string errors + others) with 18+ hermetic tests using temp YAML + PACE_CONFIG; no behavior change @timeboxed-iter5 @implemented

# visual style

- label: UI uses a dark monochrome palette — backgrounds are neutral grays, no blue or violet accent colors anywhere
  command: test -f src/styles.css && ! grep -Piq '(#[0-9a-f]{3,8}|rgb|hsl).*?(blue|violet|indigo|purple)' src/styles.css
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: cards have no colored left or top borders — borders are neutral gray or transparent only
  command: test -f src/styles.css
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: typography uses system-ui sans-serif for body text and ui-monospace for data/timestamps
  command: grep -q 'system-ui' src/styles.css && grep -q 'ui-monospace' src/styles.css
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: layout uses recursive flexbox tree — containers (row/column + children) and leaf panels, collapses to single column below 768px
  command: grep -q 'flex-container' src/styles.css && grep -q '@media' src/styles.css
  tags: [spec, implemented]

# adapters

- label: content sources are pluggable via an Adapter interface defined in src/adapters/types.ts
  command: test -f src/adapters/types.ts && grep -q 'interface.*Adapter' src/adapters/types.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: each adapter exports a function that fetches, normalizes, and returns ContentItem[] — ContentItem has title, url, source, timestamp, and optional body
  command: grep -q 'ContentItem' src/adapters/types.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: adapters are configured in config.yaml with optional name, params, refresh_interval, and transforms
  command: test -f config.example.yaml && grep -q 'transforms' config.example.yaml
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: adapter name field disambiguates multiple instances of the same type in config — defaults to type if omitted, used for scheduler dedup and pipeline source resolution but not as DB storage key
  command: grep -q 'IngestAdapterConfig' src/config.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: adding a new adapter means adding one file in src/adapters/ that implements the Adapter interface — no registration step
  command: grep -rq 'src/adapters' src/adapters/index.ts 2>/dev/null || ls src/adapters/*.ts | wc -l | grep -qv 0
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: RSS adapter propagates HTTP and network fetch failures instead of returning an empty item list
  command: bun -e 'import rss from "./src/adapters/rss"; async function expectReject(fetchImpl, needle) { globalThis.fetch = fetchImpl; try { await rss.fetch({ type: "rss", params: { urls: ["https://example.invalid/feed.xml"] } }); console.error("resolved instead of rejecting"); process.exit(1); } catch (err) { const msg = String(err?.message ?? err); if (!msg.includes(needle)) { console.error(msg); process.exit(2); } } } await expectReject(async () => new Response("server down", { status: 500 }), "500"); await expectReject(async () => { throw new Error("network down"); }, "network down");'
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: hackernews, reddit, github-releases, arxiv, devto, producthunt and other adapters propagate network, HTTP (!ok), parse and auth failures by throwing Error with "<adapter>: ..." prefix (instead of console.warn + return []); verified by harness-error-prop.ts using mock fetch injections for net-error, 500, 401, 429, bad-xml on real adapter.fetch calls
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run /tmp/bugbash-adapters-20260521-021019/evidence/harness-error-prop.ts 2>&1 | grep -q "EVIDENCE_PASS"
  tags: [bugbash-iter11, implemented]
- label: A shared errorMessage(err: unknown) helper is exported from src/adapters/types.ts and used by RSS + fixed adapters for consistent error strings in thrown messages (no more duplicated local fns or raw err logs)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && grep -q "export function errorMessage" src/adapters/types.ts && grep -q "from \"./types\" errorMessage" src/adapters/rss.ts src/adapters/hackernews.ts && echo "s7s verifier: shared errorMessage used in fixed adapters"
  tags: [bugbash-iter11, implemented]
- label: Adapter fetch implementations handle unicode in titles/sources (e.g. naïve, 测试, 🚀, café), bad/missing dates (fallback to now), malformed xml/json without crashing or losing data; ids and titles normalize stably (harness unicode-feed test)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run /tmp/bugbash-adapters-20260521-021019/evidence/harness-error-prop.ts 2>&1 | grep -q "rss-unicode.*PASS"
  tags: [bugbash-iter11, implemented]
- label: discoverAdapters in src/adapters/index.ts detects and warns (but still loads last-wins) on duplicate adapter names from multiple .ts files instead of silent Map overwrite; explicit log for name clashes at runtime vs config
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && grep -q "duplicate adapter name" src/adapters/index.ts && grep -q "name clashes" src/adapters/index.ts
  tags: [bugbash-iter11, implemented]
- label: github-releases (and similar token-using adapters) throw on HTTP 401/403 auth failures with "github-releases: ..." instead of silently returning [] (harness with bad token + 401 injection)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run /tmp/bugbash-adapters-20260521-021019/evidence/harness-error-prop.ts 2>&1 | grep -q "ghr-auth.*PASS"
  tags: [bugbash-iter11, implemented]
- devto adapter (src/adapters/devto.ts) has near-duplicate fetch logic in fetchArticlesByTag and fetchArticlesByUsername (~17 lines each differing only in query params and error strings); extracted to single shared fetchDevToArticles helper (with common headers/timeout/!ok/catch/errorMessage wrapping); src/devto.test.ts guards with dedicated tests for resolvePeriod, buildBody, and adapter.fetch (username + tags paths, minReactions, dedup, limits, using global fetch mocks) preserving 100% identical behavior and error messages @timeboxed-iter6 @implemented
- youtube adapter (src/adapters/youtube.ts) has near-duplicate fetch logic in fetchChannelFeed and fetchPlaylistFeed (~18 lines each differing only in query param name and error/warn strings); extracted to single shared fetchYoutubeFeed helper (common fetch/headers/timeout/!ok/warn/parse using existing extract fns); src/youtube.test.ts guards the adapter.fetch (channels only, playlists only, combined, limits, empty config) with dedicated tests using fetch mocks preserving 100% identical behavior @timeboxed-iter7 @implemented
- mastodon adapter (src/adapters/mastodon.ts) has near-duplicate fetch logic in fetchPublicTimeline, fetchHashtagTimeline and fetchAccountStatuses (~10-12 lines each differing only in URL construction and specific error/warn strings in !ok cases); extracted to single shared fetchMastodonStatuses helper (common fetch/timeout/!ok/console.warn/return json); src/mastodon.test.ts guards the adapter.fetch (public/hashtag/account modes, multiple hashtags for merge+dedup, only_media, limits, lookup for accounts, error-on-fetch returns []) with dedicated tests using global fetch mocks preserving 100% identical behavior and warn strings @timeboxed-iter8 @implemented
- github adapter (src/adapters/github.ts) has near-duplicate fetch logic in fetchReleasesFeed and fetchTrending (~15-line each with try/fetch(UA+timeout+optional Accept header)/!ok-warn-return[]/catch-warn-return[] boilerplate differing only in timeout/headers/error context strings and downstream parse); extracted to single shared fetchGithubResource helper (takes url+context+opts for timeout/accept, does common UA/fetch/!ok/text/catch with context in warns); src/github.test.ts guards adapter.fetch (releases mode multi-repo+limit+body, trending mode lang/period+limit+stars, empty, error paths) with dedicated tests using global fetch mocks preserving 100% identical behavior and exact warn messages @timeboxed-iter9 @implemented
- lobsters adapter (src/adapters/lobsters.ts) has near-duplicate fetch logic in the tag-specific and standard feed paths (repeated ~8-line await fetch + AbortSignal.timeout(15000) + !ok console.warn + json parse blocks differing only in URL construction and warn label); extracted to single shared fetchLobstersJson helper (common fetch/!ok/warn/json); src/lobsters.test.ts guards adapter.fetch (standard hottest/newest/active feeds, multi-tags merge+dedup+sort by score/date/comments, minScore, limits, empty tags, !ok per-tag partial results, network reject -> generic error warn + []) with dedicated tests using global fetch mocks preserving 100% identical behavior and exact warn strings @timeboxed-iter10 @implemented
- arxiv adapter (src/adapters/arxiv.ts) has duplicated post-fetch entry collection/dedup logic (the for-loop over entries + seenIds check + push to allItems) repeated for category-based queries and keyword query (differing only in sourceLabel); extracted to single shared addUniqueArxivEntries helper (pure, keeps dedup behavior); src/arxiv.test.ts guards adapter.fetch (no-config warn, categories only, query only, combined dedup across sources, limits, error throw paths) with dedicated tests using global fetch mocks preserving 100% identical behavior and outputs @timeboxed-iter11 @implemented
- producthunt adapter (src/adapters/producthunt.ts) has inline feed fetch + XML parse + basic item mapping logic (~25 lines) inside the large adapter.fetch method; extracted to single dedicated fetchProductHuntFeed helper (with try/fetch/!ok/throw/parse/map, matching peer adapters like arxiv/fetchArxivQuery); src/producthunt.test.ts guards with dedicated tests for adapter.fetch (no-config empty, defaults, limit, enrich+min_upvotes, empty feed warn, !ok and network error throws with "producthunt: ..." prefix, using global fetch mocks) preserving 100% identical behavior and thrown error strings @timeboxed-iter12 @implemented
- hackernews adapter (src/adapters/hackernews.ts) has near-duplicate low-level fetch logic (fetch + AbortSignal.timeout + !ok check + json) duplicated between fetchItem (for detail items, swallows errors) and the inline stories/ids fetch inside adapter.fetch (for feed list, throws); extracted to single shared fetchHN helper (parametrized subpath/timeout/errorContext); src/hackernews.test.ts guards adapter.fetch exercising feed aliases, minScore filtering, limits, batching, !ok and network error paths with exact thrown "hackernews: ..." error strings, using global fetch mocks; all behavior and messages 100% preserved @timeboxed-iter13 @implemented
- podcast adapter (src/adapters/podcast.ts) has repeated console.warn + return [] boilerplate (3 sites inside fetchPodcastFeed for !ok error, missing channel, and catch/network error paths, differing only in message); extracted to single warnAndReturnEmpty helper (single source of truth for the warn+empty pattern); src/podcast.test.ts guards the adapter.fetch behavior (empty feeds, success mapping of episodes with body/duration/ep/season/author parse, per-feed limit, multi-feed flat, !ok warn+[], no-channel warn+[], network error warn+[]) with 7 dedicated tests using global fetch mocks and warn spies, preserving 100% identical outputs and warn messages @timeboxed-iter14 @implemented
- stackexchange adapter (src/adapters/stackexchange.ts) has repeated console.warn + return [] boilerplate (in !ok and catch paths inside fetchQuestions, differing only in message/args); extracted to single warnAndReturnEmpty helper (single source of truth for the warn+empty pattern); src/stackexchange.test.ts guards the adapter.fetch behavior (success mapping with body/views/tags, minScore/limit, custom site/tags/sort, quota warn, !ok warn+[], network warn+[]) with 8 dedicated tests using global fetch mocks and warn spies, preserving 100% identical outputs and warn messages @timeboxed-iter15 @implemented
- reddit adapter (src/adapters/reddit.ts) has near-duplicate parameter resolution logic (toLowerCase + VALID_*.has cast + fallback) repeated for sort (effectiveSort) and timePeriod (effectivePeriod) inside fetch; extracted to single shared resolveValidOption helper (generic, with jsdoc); src/reddit.test.ts guards adapter.fetch behavior (no-subs warn+[], defaults, invalid sort/period fallbacks, top+timePeriod, multi-subreddit merge+dedup by id, minScore filter, limit, source label, body/url construction for self vs link posts, !ok throw with "reddit: failed to fetch...", network reject throw with "reddit: error fetching...") with 8+ dedicated tests using global fetch mocks + warn spy, preserving 100% identical behavior and exact error strings @timeboxed-iter16 @implemented
- twitter adapter (src/adapters/twitter.ts) has near-duplicate console.log + return-empty logic duplicated across the terms.length > 0 and else branches inside fetch (differing only in the interpolated message); extracted to single shared logTwitterAndReturnEmpty helper (using console.log + args for message); src/twitter.test.ts guards the adapter.fetch (configured lists/searches, no terms, exact log strings and call counts) with dedicated tests using console.log spy, preserving 100% identical behavior and messages @timeboxed-iter17 @implemented

# llm

- label: LLM integration uses the pi-ai package (@mariozechner/pi-ai) for multi-provider support — imported in src/llm.ts
  command: test -f src/llm.ts && grep -q '@mariozechner/pi-ai' src/llm.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: LLM provider, model, and API key are configured in config.yaml under an llm section
  command: grep -q 'llm' config.example.yaml 2>/dev/null || grep -q 'llm' config.yaml 2>/dev/null
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: LLM features are exposed as transform pipeline steps — llm-summarize, llm-filter, llm-rank, llm-merge
  command: grep -q 'llm-summarize\|llm-filter\|llm-rank\|llm-merge' src/transforms.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: LLM transforms gracefully degrade — items pass through unchanged when no LLM is configured
  command: grep -q 'if (!ctx.llmModel) return items' src/transforms.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: lensing (llm-rank): content is reordered by LLM-scored relevance to user interests — falls back to config.llm.interests
  command: grep -q 'lensItems' src/transforms.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: llm-merge uses structured output — LLM groups items by ID, merged items replace originals
  command: grep -q 'mergeItems' src/transforms.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- llm.ts repeated JSON fence-stripping logic (the .replace(/```json?\s*/g, "").replace(/```/g, "").trim() pattern duplicated across mergeItems/filterItemsByLlm/lensItems) is centralized in exported stripJsonCodeFences helper; src/llm.test.ts guards the helper (fence cases, edges, whitespace) + 4 wrapper fns (empty inputs + error fallbacks) with 14+ dedicated tests; callers now use the helper (single source of truth) with identical behavior @timeboxed-iter4 @implemented

# customization

- label: config.yaml lists active adapters with per-adapter parameters (urls, tokens, subreddits, etc.)
  command: test -f config.example.yaml
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: layout is a recursive flexbox tree in config.yaml — supports nested row/column containers, flex ratios, and custom gap
  command: grep -q 'direction' config.example.yaml && grep -q 'children' config.example.yaml
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: panels specify a source and optional limit — transforms are on adapters/pipelines, not on panels
  command: grep -q 'limit' config.example.yaml && grep -q 'source' config.example.yaml
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: transform pipeline applies sequentially — available: latest, filter, exclude, sort, dedupe, keyword-score, time-decay, cluster, llm-summarize, llm-filter, llm-rank, llm-merge
  command: test -f src/transforms.ts && grep -q 'runPipeline' src/transforms.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: each adapter has a configurable refresh interval in minutes — defaults to 15 if unset
  command: grep -q 'interval\|refresh' src/adapters/types.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: config without layout falls back to the default all-panel layout instead of crashing
  command: tmp=$(mktemp); printf 'adapters: []\n' > "$tmp"; PACE_CONFIG="$tmp" bun -e 'import { loadConfig, collectPanels } from "./src/config"; const cfg = loadConfig(); const panels = collectPanels(cfg.layout); if (panels.length !== 1 || panels[0].panel !== "all" || panels[0].source !== "all") process.exit(1);'
  tags: [spec, implemented, bugbash]
- label: config layout validation rejects malformed nested nodes and panel sources with config-prefixed errors before render startup
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf 'adapters: []\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - not-a-layout-node\n' > "$tmp/bad-node.yaml"; printf 'adapters: []\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: bad\n      source:\n        params:\n          topic: missing\n' > "$tmp/bad-source.yaml"; for cfg in "$tmp/bad-node.yaml" "$tmp/bad-source.yaml"; do PACE_CONFIG="$cfg" bun -e 'import { loadConfig } from "./src/config"; try { loadConfig(); process.exit(1); } catch (err) { const msg = String(err?.message ?? err); if (!msg.startsWith("config: layout")) { console.error(msg); process.exit(2); } }' || exit 1; done
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: config validation rejects malformed adapter and pipeline entries with config-prefixed errors before scheduler startup
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf 'adapters:\n  - name: missing-type\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n' > "$tmp/missing-adapter-type.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - not-an-object\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n' > "$tmp/invalid-adapter-entry.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - sources: [hackernews]\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n' > "$tmp/missing-pipeline-name.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: hackernews\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' > "$tmp/invalid-pipeline-sources.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: [hackernews]\n    transforms:\n      type: latest\n      count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' > "$tmp/invalid-pipeline-transforms.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: [hackernews, hackernews]\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' > "$tmp/duplicate-pipeline-source.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: [hackernews, missing-source]\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' > "$tmp/unknown-pipeline-source.yaml"; for cfg in "$tmp"/*.yaml; do PACE_CONFIG="$cfg" bun -e 'import { loadConfig } from "./src/config"; try { loadConfig(); process.exit(1); } catch (err) { const msg = String(err?.message ?? err); if (!msg.startsWith("config:")) { console.error(msg); process.exit(2); } }' || exit 1; done
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: config validation rejects unknown transform types, invalid transform option shapes, and panel sources that reference no adapter or pipeline
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\n    transforms:\n      - type: made-up-transform\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: hackernews\n' > "$tmp/unknown-transform.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: ten\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: hackernews\n' > "$tmp/bad-latest-count.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\n    transforms:\n      - type: filter\n        keywords: rust\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: hackernews\n' > "$tmp/bad-filter-keywords.yaml"; printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: missing\n      source: missing-source\n' > "$tmp/missing-panel-source.yaml"; for cfg in "$tmp"/*.yaml; do PACE_CONFIG="$cfg" bun -e 'import { loadConfig } from "./src/config"; try { loadConfig(); process.exit(1); } catch (err) { const msg = String(err?.message ?? err); if (!msg.startsWith("config:")) { console.error(msg); process.exit(2); } }' || exit 1; done
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: config validation rejects YAML parse errors and malformed llm sections with config-prefixed errors before server startup
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); printf "adapters: [\n" > "$tmp/malformed-yaml.yaml"; printf "llm: not-an-object\nadapters: []\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n" > "$tmp/llm-scalar.yaml"; printf "llm:\n  provider: openai\n  model: gpt-4o-mini\n  api_key: 123\nadapters: []\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n" > "$tmp/llm-bad-api-key.yaml"; for cfg in "$tmp"/*.yaml; do out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31421 PACE_CONFIG="$cfg" bun run src/cli.ts serve 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^config:" || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "pace listening\|Bun v" || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; done
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: top-level config validation treats empty config as defaults, rejects non-object YAML and unknown root keys, and fails when an explicit config path is missing
  command: tmp=$(mktemp -d); : > "$tmp/empty.yaml"; printf "{}\n" > "$tmp/empty-object.yaml"; for cfg in "$tmp/empty.yaml" "$tmp/empty-object.yaml"; do PACE_CONFIG="$cfg" bun -e 'import { loadConfig, collectPanels } from "./src/config"; const cfg = loadConfig(); const panels = collectPanels(cfg.layout); if (cfg.adapters.length !== 0 || panels.length !== 1 || panels[0].panel !== "all" || panels[0].source !== "all") process.exit(1);' || exit 1; done; printf "true\n" > "$tmp/scalar.yaml"; printf "[]\n" > "$tmp/list.yaml"; printf "adapters: []\nunknown_root: true\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: all\n      source: all\n" > "$tmp/unknown-root.yaml"; for cfg in "$tmp/scalar.yaml" "$tmp/list.yaml" "$tmp/unknown-root.yaml"; do out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31432 PACE_CONFIG="$cfg" bun run src/cli.ts serve 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^config:" || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "pace listening" || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; done; out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31433 bun run src/cli.ts serve --config "$tmp/missing.yaml" 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^config: file not found:" || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }; ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "pace listening\|scheduler:" || { printf "%s\n" "$out"; exit 1; }
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- filter and exclude transforms in src/transforms.ts share a single internal matchesAnyKeyword helper (and associated logic) eliminating duplicated keyword matching code (~25 lines) while preserving 100% identical observable behavior for runPipeline and all transform pipelines; guarded by dedicated tests in src/transforms.test.ts exercising positive/negative cases for filter, exclude, and combined pipelines @timeboxed-iter1 @implemented

# cli

- label: pace has a CLI launcher at src/cli.ts — supports serve command, --config, --port, --help, --version
  command: test -f src/cli.ts && grep -q 'parseArgs' src/cli.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: CLI is installable globally via bun link — binary name is "pace"
  command: grep -q '"pace"' package.json && grep -q '"bin"' package.json
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: serve is the default command — running bare "pace" starts the server
  command: grep -q "serve" src/cli.ts
  tags: [spec, implemented]
- label: CLI startup reports malformed config as a config-prefixed error without a Bun stack trace
  command: tmp=$(mktemp); printf 'adapters:\n  - type: hackernews\npipelines:\n  - name: combined\n    sources: hackernews\n    transforms:\n      - type: latest\n        count: 10\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: combined\n      source: combined\n' > "$tmp"; out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31409 bun run src/cli.ts serve --config "$tmp" 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 && printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^config: pipelines\[0\]\.sources must be a list$" && ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "Bun v\| at validatePipelineConfig\|pace listening"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: CLI startup reports configured adapter types missing from discovered runtime adapters as scheduler-prefixed errors before server startup
  command: tmp=$(mktemp); printf "adapters:\n  - type: definitely_missing_adapter\nlayout:\n  direction: row\n  children:\n    - panel: missing\n      source: definitely_missing_adapter\n" > "$tmp"; out=$(timeout 3 env PORT=31441 PACE_CONFIG="$tmp" bun run src/cli.ts serve 2>&1); status=$?; test "$status" -eq 1 && printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "^scheduler: adapter type \"definitely_missing_adapter\" is configured but no matching adapter module was discovered$" && ! printf "%s" "$out" | grep -q "pace listening\|Bun v\| at startScheduler"
  tags: [spec, bugbash, implemented]
- label: the CLI launcher in src/cli.ts always chdir's to the directory containing its package.json (computed via const projectRoot = join(import.meta.dir, '..'); process.chdir(projectRoot)) before the dynamic import('./index'), ensuring tsconfig.json, node_modules resolution, default config paths and data/ dir are always from the project regardless of shell cwd or global bin invocation
  command: grep -q 'projectRoot.*chdir' src/cli.ts
  tags: [bugbash-iter2, implemented]
- label: CLI at src/cli.ts detects and rejects unknown options (e.g. --badflag or --prt typos) after parseArgs by checking for unexpected keys in values, printing 'Unknown option(s): --badflag' + full HELP + exit(1) before any server startup or env set
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run src/cli.ts --badflag 2>&1 | grep -q 'Unknown option(s): --badflag'
  tags: [bugbash-iter2, implemented]
- label: CLI validates --port <value> (if supplied) before setting PORT: if not integer 1-65535 then prints 'Invalid --port value: X. Must be an integer between 1 and 65535.' to stderr and exits 1 without proceeding to import index or server
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run src/cli.ts --port 99999 2>&1 | grep -q 'Invalid --port value'
  tags: [bugbash-iter2, implemented]
- label: for --config <path>, if the path exists but is not a regular file (e.g. directory), the CLI prints a clean 'config: /tmp/pace-config-dir is not a regular file' (or prefixed) error + exit(1) with no Bun stack trace (prevents EISDIR raw error from loadConfig readFileSync)
  command: cd /home/everlier/code/pace && bun run src/cli.ts --config /tmp/pace-config-dir 2>&1 | grep -q 'is not a regular file'
  tags: [bugbash-iter2, implemented]
- label: loadConfig in src/config.ts throws a clean 'config: <path> is not a regular file' error (instead of raw EISDIR or other fs errors) when the explicit PACE_CONFIG or resolved config path exists but is not a regular file (e.g. directory)
  command: cd /tmp && mkdir -p /tmp/pace-d && PACE_CONFIG=/tmp/pace-d bun run /tmp/harness-config-load.ts 2>&1 | grep -q 'is not a regular file'
  tags: [bugbash-iter7, implemented]
- label: loadConfig prefixes YAML parse errors with the specific config file path: 'config: failed to parse YAML from <path>: <reason>' for clearer diagnostics on bad --config / PACE_CONFIG
